## Phase 6: User Story 4 - Heartbeat Monitoring & Health Tracking

**User Story**: As a service owner, I want my service to send heartbeats so that the platform can track its health status automatically.

**Scenarios**: Scenario 6 (Healthy Status), Scenario 7 (Health Degrades), Scenario 8 (Degraded Recovers), Scenario 9 (Dead Recovers)

**Test Criteria**:
- ✅ POST /api/v1/heartbeat/{serviceId} responds with ACK within 500ms
- ✅ Background service detects missed heartbeats and transitions status: HEALTHY → UNHEALTHY → DEGRADED → DEAD
- ✅ Service status transitions to RECOVERED when heartbeats resume after DEAD
- ✅ Service status transitions to HEALTHY after consecutive successful heartbeats in RECOVERED state
- ✅ Heartbeat writes optimized (write only on status change or periodic snapshot)
- ✅ Background service polls every 5 seconds to check for timeout

### Tasks

#### Business Logic

- [ ] T100 [US4] Create `HeartbeatService` in `src/Omni.ServiceRegistry.Services/HeartbeatService.cs` implementing IHeartbeatService with ConcurrentDictionary for in-memory state
- [ ] T101 [US4] Implement ProcessHeartbeatAsync in HeartbeatService: update in-memory heartbeat state, calculate health status, conditionally write to database (status change or periodic snapshot per MaxMissedHeartbeats)
- [ ] T102 [US4] Implement health status calculation logic: determine new status based on MissedHeartbeatCounter and MaxMissedHeartbeats thresholds (0=HEALTHY, >0 and <50%=UNHEALTHY, ≥50%=DEGRADED, >max=DEAD)
- [ ] T103 [US4] Create `HeartbeatMonitorService` BackgroundService in `src/Omni.ServiceRegistry.Services/HeartbeatMonitorService.cs` that polls every 5 seconds
- [ ] T104 [US4] Implement ExecuteAsync in HeartbeatMonitorService: query all services, check if LastHeartbeatTimestamp + HeartbeatTimeout < now, increment MissedHeartbeatCounter, update health status, log warnings/errors
- [ ] T105 [US4] Implement GetServiceHealthAsync in HeartbeatService: retrieve Service from repository, return current health status and last heartbeat timestamp

#### API Layer

- [ ] T106 [P] [US4] Create `HeartbeatRequestDto` in `src/Omni.ServiceRegistry.Api/DTOs/HeartbeatRequestDto.cs` with ClientStatus property
- [ ] T107 [P] [US4] Create `HeartbeatResponseDto` in `src/Omni.ServiceRegistry.Api/DTOs/HeartbeatResponseDto.cs` with Acknowledged property
- [ ] T108 [P] [US4] Create `ServiceStatusDto` in `src/Omni.ServiceRegistry.Api/DTOs/ServiceStatusDto.cs` with ServiceId, ServiceName, HealthStatus, LastHeartbeatTimestamp properties
- [ ] T109 [US4] Create `HeartbeatController` in `src/Omni.ServiceRegistry.Api/Controllers/HeartbeatController.cs` with POST /api/v1/heartbeat/{serviceId} endpoint
- [ ] T110 [US4] Implement POST /heartbeat/{serviceId} endpoint: accept HeartbeatRequestDto, call HeartbeatService.ProcessHeartbeatAsync, return HeartbeatResponseDto with HTTP 200 (must respond <500ms)
- [ ] T111 [US4] Add rate limiting to heartbeat endpoint in Program.cs: fixed window policy, 200 requests/second, queue size 50
- [ ] T112 [US4] Implement GET /api/v1/status/service/{id} endpoint in StatusController: call HeartbeatService.GetServiceHealthAsync, return ServiceStatusDto with HTTP 200 or HTTP 404
- [ ] T113 [US4] Register HeartbeatMonitorService as hosted service in Program.cs

#### Storage Layer Extensions

- [ ] T114 [P] [US4] Implement UpdateAsync in PostgresServiceRepository with optimistic concurrency handling (catch DbUpdateConcurrencyException, reload, retry)
- [ ] T115 [P] [US4] Implement UpdateAsync in RedisServiceRepository (last write wins)
- [ ] T116 [P] [US4] Implement UpdateAsync in FileServiceRepository with file locking

#### Integration

- [ ] T117 [US4] Approve a service registration from Phase 4 to create a Service entity for testing
- [ ] T118 [US4] Test POST /api/v1/heartbeat/{serviceId} with valid serviceId: verify returns ACK within 500ms
- [ ] T119 [US4] Test POST /api/v1/heartbeat/{serviceId} multiple times: verify service remains HEALTHY
- [ ] T120 [US4] Stop sending heartbeats and wait for timeout: verify status transitions to UNHEALTHY, then DEGRADED, then DEAD (via GET /status/service/{id})
- [ ] T121 [US4] Resume heartbeats after DEAD: verify status transitions to RECOVERED, then HEALTHY after consecutive successes
- [ ] T122 [US4] Verify heartbeat writes are optimized: check database for reduced write count (status changes + periodic snapshots only)

