## Phase 8: User Story 6 - Service Deletion Workflow

**User Story**: As a service owner or administrator, I want to request service deletion so that obsolete services are removed from the catalog.

**Scenarios**: Scenario 10 (Service Deletion)

**Test Criteria**:
- ✅ POST /api/v1/delete/{id} marks service with DeletionStatus=PendingDeletion
- ✅ Administrator can approve deletion via POST /api/v1/admin/delete/{id}/approve
- ✅ Approved deletion marks service with DeletionStatus=Deleted
- ✅ Deleted services are excluded from catalog queries (soft-delete filter)
- ✅ Deleted service can be re-registered with new service ID

### Tasks

- [ ] T137 [US6] Extend AdministratorService with DeleteServiceAsync method: validate service exists, mark DeletionStatus=PendingDeletion, log deletion request
- [ ] T138 [US6] Extend AdministratorService with ApproveDeletionAsync method: validate service exists and is PendingDeletion, mark DeletionStatus=Deleted, log approval
- [ ] T139 [P] [US6] Create `DeletionRequestDto` in `src/Omni.ServiceRegistry.Api/DTOs/DeletionRequestDto.cs` with Reason property
- [ ] T140 [US6] Implement POST /api/v1/delete/{id} endpoint in AdminController: accept DeletionRequestDto, call AdministratorService.DeleteServiceAsync, return HTTP 200
- [ ] T141 [US6] Implement POST /api/v1/admin/delete/{id}/approve endpoint in AdminController: call AdministratorService.ApproveDeletionAsync, return HTTP 200
- [ ] T142 [US6] Test POST /api/v1/delete/{id}: verify DeletionStatus changes to PendingDeletion
- [ ] T143 [US6] Test POST /api/v1/admin/delete/{id}/approve: verify DeletionStatus changes to Deleted
- [ ] T144 [US6] Test catalog query excludes deleted service: verify GET /api/v1/services does not return deleted service
- [ ] T145 [US6] Test re-registration after deletion: submit new registration with same service name, verify new registration ID is assigned

